# Create a Serving Signature

We need a function that accepts raw strings (or token ids) and returns probabilities. Here we'll create a signature that takes integer sequences and outputs sentiment.

```python
@tf.function(input_signature=[tf.TensorSpec(shape=[None, maxlen], dtype=tf.int32, name='input_text')])
def serve_fn(input_text):
    return model(input_text)

tf.saved_model.save(model, 'sentiment_model/1/', signatures={'serving_default': serve_fn})
```
